  "layer5_verifier_fairness_static__verifier_execution_completeness": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The entrypoint chain test.sh -> test_gvs.sh -> test_outputs.py main() -> _emit_engine_owned_reward -> score_benchmark_verifiers -> run_benchmark_verifiers dispatches every manifest verifier; unsupported types would be marked unscored and make the run ungradable rather than silently skipped, and an infrastructure failure raises instead of emitting a zero. evaluations/oracle/verifier/verifier_summary.json shows total 75, passed 75, unscored 0, failure_mode 'pass', with per-type scores for file_check and database_state — i.e. every declared check actually executed."
  },
  "layer5_verifier_fairness_static__score_bucket_activation": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The active bucket is the flat engine pool (flat_verifier_scoring=true): 75 weighted items summing to ~1.004. The state and sql axes are reported enabled:false (expected_diff.json is {} and state_snapshot_enabled=false), so they are not represented as coverage. rubric.toml declares no criteria, so no empty judge bucket is counted; the legacy 'rubric' block in reward.json merely carries the engine's own 75 items. No zero-weight or unreachable verifier exists (minimum weight 0.004098, every one evidenced in the recorded run)."
  },
  "layer5_verifier_fairness_static__aggregation_normalization": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "With flat_verifier_scoring the score is sum(weight of passed)/sum(weight). Recomputed weights: 2x0.14 + 5x0.03 + 2x0.02 + 0.08 + 61x~0.004098 + 0.00412 + 4x0.05 = 1.0041, so an all-pass run yields 1.0 — matching evaluations/oracle (reward.txt 1.0, result.json rewards {'reward': 1.0}). A documents-only run computes to 0.56 and a hedge-all removal world to ~0.12, consistent with the mutation suite's '<= 0.2' note. scoring.weights (rubric 1.0, others 0) is display-only on this path and does not contradict the effective math, and 'pass' is core-based (all 75) rather than a threshold."
  },
  "layer5_verifier_fairness_static__scoring_proportionality": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "Weight tracks materiality: the two full registers 0.14 each, the memo table 0.08, the five summary figures 0.03 each, the cosmetic one-page cap only 0.02, the 61 individual remediations ~0.25 in total, and the four correctness locks 0.20. No cosmetic item dominates. The locks deliberately read -1 until all 61 fixes are in place, so one missed fix costs 0.204 rather than 0.004 — a sharp but documented and necessary design (otherwise a do-nothing agent would collect the three 'untouched' locks for free), and the metadata on each lock states this precondition explicitly."
  },
  "layer5_verifier_fairness_static__check_independence": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The 61 per-grant checks each read a distinct permission id; the three tier locks read disjoint sets of allowed grants and the fourth reads Drive-wide tallies. The overlap — all four locks are additionally gated on the same 61-fix predicate — is disclosed verbatim in each lock's why_justification ('Counted only once every one of the 61 fixes is in place (-1 before that), so partial work never earns it'), and serves a distinct purpose (precision cannot be bought without recall). No other check pair rewards the same fact twice."
  },
  "layer5_verifier_fairness_static__counterfactual_strength": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The matchers themselves distinguish the cases: positive (oracle artifacts + writes = 1.0, recorded in evaluations/oracle); negative (swapped tier/action, every summary figure off by one, every People count off by one fail precisely their own check); incomplete (a missing spreadsheet, grant or memo row fails the row_set multiset lock; a missing fix fails its grant check and all four locks); adversarial (invented rows, one row naming every id, hedge rows fail the population/row locks; do-nothing scores 0 on all state checks; hedge-all removal fails the three untouched locks). consistency/mutations.json documents 43 such cases with all controls passing, consistent with my own reading of compare.table_equals and the SQL."
  },
  "layer5_verifier_fairness_static__process_grading_justification": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "No reward depends on workflow or trace shape: trajectory scoring is inactive on the engine path, forbidden_tools is empty, and the evidence passed to the engine is used only to build a model_response whose tool_calls no verifier reads. Reward comes solely from the requested outcomes — the Drive permission end state and the two documents."
  },
  "layer5_llm_judge_design": {
    "outcome": "not_applicable",
    "explanation": "No LLM judge grades anything in this task. tests/rubric.toml declares only a [system] preamble and no criteria, so _rubric_check_verifiers_from_rubric yields zero verifiers, and the 75 manifest verifier_configs are all file_check or database_state. The oracle run confirms it: 65 database_state + 10 file_check items, no judge item. (Noted, not scored here: score_benchmark_verifiers still requires metadata.verifier_judge and a non-empty OPENAI_API_KEY to exist, and a missing key raises rather than emitting a zero, so the degenerate case fails loudly as UNSCORED.)"
  },
  "layer5_llm_judge_design__judge_execution_validity": {
    "outcome": "not_applicable",
    "explanation": "No judge call is made during grading — there are no rubric items and no response_check/rubric_check verifiers, so model id, endpoint, request and parsing are never exercised for reward."
  },
  "layer5_llm_judge_design__judge_failure_handling": {
    "outcome": "not_applicable",
    "explanation": "No judge is invoked. For completeness, _emit_engine_owned_reward raises on any judge/infrastructure error instead of converting it to a zero, so the degenerate configuration would be recorded as unscored, not as an agent mistake."
  },
  "layer5_llm_judge_design__judge_context_completeness": {
    "outcome": "not_applicable",
    "explanation": "No judge prompt is constructed because rubric.toml declares no criteria."
  },
  "layer5_llm_judge_design__judge_context_truncation": {
    "outcome": "not_applicable",
    "explanation": "No judge context is built; the rubric evidence block (max_chars 350000) is never used on this scoring path."
  },
  "layer5_llm_judge_design__artifact_grounding": {
    "outcome": "not_applicable",
    "explanation": "No judge rubric language exists; all grading is deterministic against the produced artifacts and the gym database."
  },
  "layer5_llm_judge_design__repeat_stability": {
    "outcome": "not_applicable",
    "explanation": "No judge sampling occurs, so there is nothing stochastic to stabilise; the 75 deterministic checks are reproducible."
  },
  "layer5_reward_hacking_static": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "All four exploitability subchecks pass: fabricated or lazy rollouts cannot satisfy the keyed population locks or the Drive-wide state assertions, the only mutation path is the sanctioned gws connector, the answer key and golden solution are unreadable to the agent, and grading state is not writable by the agent."
  },
  "layer5_reward_hacking_static__rollout_legitimacy": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "Reward is final-surface based, but the surfaces are not fabricable: the registers must contain exactly the right 70 ids with the right tiers, the right 61 permission ids with the right actions and the right 26 post-change head-counts, all of which require actually reading each spreadsheet's tabs and applying the policy; and 65 SQL checks read the real Drive permission rows, so claiming changes without making them scores zero on 0.449 of the weight and fails 'pass'. Destructive behaviour is penalised: removing or re-roling an allowed grant, or touching any other file, breaks the four locks."
  },
  "layer5_reward_hacking_static__sanctioned_interface_use": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The agent's only reachable surfaces are the proxy's public /mcp/{server} and /cli/{name} routes (command input validated by _validated_bridge_command, identity limited to the x-gws-auth-token header). The raw /raw/{name}/state and /raw/{name}/step endpoints live on a separate Starlette app bound to a 0600 root-owned unix socket and additionally require a root-only capability file, so no direct database or verifier access exists. Connector state under /gyms is chmod 710 root:gym and unreadable to rlgymagent."
  },
  "layer5_reward_hacking_static__golden_or_internal_access": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "solution/ is never copied into the image; the expectations live in /app/tests/manifest.json inside a tree the Dockerfile makes root-only (chmod -R go-rwx /app), and the proxy's mirrored copy is root:harborproxy 0640. /logs/verifier is root 0700 and is pre-created by the entrypoint so the agent cannot pre-seed or symlink it. The agent-visible /workspace holds only the three legitimate input fixtures, which contain no answers (they are the policy, roster and exception register the task expects the agent to apply)."
  },
  "layer5_reward_hacking_static__state_spoofing": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The documents are the deliverable, so their being agent-written is expected; they are checked against fixed keyed expectations rather than against anything the agent controls. Drive state is read by SQL from the gym database the agent cannot write except through the connector, each check pins a specific permission id plus role and file_id (not a count that a compensating change could fake), and the Drive-wide tallies plus the owner count catch additions, deletions and re-roles elsewhere. Seeded state cannot satisfy the checks: each per-grant query is documented to read 0 on the pre-run seed and each lock to read -1, so a passing value can only come from work actually done during the run."
  }
}

