  "layer5_verifier_fairness_static__surface_form_brittleness": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "I inspected every matcher. id_pattern '(?i)([0-9a-f]{8}-...)' and '(?i)\\b(perm_[a-z]+_\\d+)\\b' extract the canonical token from a decorated cell; the Summary id_pattern '^[\\s*_:\\-]*(.*?)[\\s*_:.\\-]*$' strips markdown bullets/emphasis/colons around a measure label; the memo header_match '(?i)spreadsheet\\W*id\\W*\\|.*people' matches the joined header row with positional column keys so a reworded second header still reads. None of these can be gamed by mimicking tokens: a row that names every id at once, or extra invented rows, fail the row_set multiset lock (consistency/mutations.json records exactly those adversarial cases failing). No matcher checks less than its criterion claims — each grades the full keyed population it describes."
